  "gradeRuleDescribe": {
    "yms_year": 114.0,
    "yms_smester": 2.0,
    "cls_id": "NM04110",
    "sub_id": "97860",
    "scr_dup": "001",
    "tpa_score_new": "<div>Grades given&nbsp;</div>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": "<div>In-class work/Class Participation....20% Other Assignments....20% Mid-term assignments (2)....30% (15% each) Final....30%</div>\n",
    "course_pol": "Students are expected to arrive to class on time.\nStudents are encouraged to bring a laptop computer or tablet with which to do in-class assignments. \nAssignments must be turned in on time. The teacher reserves the right to not accept any late assignments. \nTwo absences or less will not affect student grades. Students are responsible for communication and arrangements for additional absences.",
    "course_pol_en": "Course Policies\nStudents are expected to show up on time and ready to work. Students are strongly encouraged to bring a laptop to class, though a tablet with keyboard will work in a pinch.  Assignments will be accepted late at a penalty of 20%. Assignments will not be accepted more than two weeks after the original due date except in the case of truly extenuating circumstances.",
    "course_rem": "LLMs can be an excellent tool to aid you in your journey as a writer. At present, they cannot replace humans, and misuse or overuse of this tool will only be denying yourself a learning opportunity.\nPlagiarism is unacceptable. Learning to cite properly is one of the primary goals of this course.",
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<div>Students are expected to complete their work on time and by themselves. Appropriate use of outside learning aids (Grammarly, ChatGPT, other LLMs) is acceptable under circumstances outlined in class. Assignments found to be plagiarized will result in a 0. To avoid plagiarism, follow the APA citation guidelines as taught during this course.&nbsp;&nbsp;</div>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Students are expected to complete all of&nbsp;their own work and provide citations as needed (no restriction on formatting). Violations of academic integrity will be judged on a case-by-case basis. A first violation will generally result in a 0 on the assignment, a second violation with a harsher penalty, and a third violation will generally result in a 0 in the course.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": null
  },
